### ==========================================================================
### Azure OpenAI Response API — Cross-Instance State Test (.http)
###
### Uses the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
###
### Part A: AI Services (Foundry) Instances
###   1. POST /openai/v1/responses  → Instance 1: Create response, capture ID
###   2. GET  /openai/v1/responses/{{responseId}} → Instance 2: Retrieve by ID
###
### Part B: Azure OpenAI (kind: OpenAI) Instances
###   3. POST /openai/v1/responses  → OpenAI 1: Create response, capture ID
###   4. GET  /openai/v1/responses/{{oaiResponseId}} → OpenAI 2: Retrieve by ID
### ==========================================================================

### ── Variables (AI Services / Foundry) ────────────────────────────────

@instance1 = {{$dotenv AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT_1}}
@apiKey1   = {{$dotenv AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY_1}}

@instance2 = {{$dotenv AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT_2}}
@apiKey2   = {{$dotenv AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY_2}}

@model = {{$dotenv AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_NAME}}

### ── Variables (Azure OpenAI) ─────────────────────────────────────────

@oaiInstance1 = {{$dotenv AZURE_OAI_ENDPOINT_1}}
@oaiApiKey1   = {{$dotenv AZURE_OAI_API_KEY_1}}

@oaiInstance2 = {{$dotenv AZURE_OAI_ENDPOINT_2}}
@oaiApiKey2   = {{$dotenv AZURE_OAI_API_KEY_2}}

@oaiInstance3 = {{$dotenv AZURE_OAI_ENDPOINT_3}}
@oaiApiKey3   = {{$dotenv AZURE_OAI_API_KEY_3}}


### ==========================================================================
### PART A: AI Services (Foundry) Instances
### ==========================================================================

### ==========================================================================
### STEP 1 — Create a response on AI Services Instance 1
### ==========================================================================

# @name createResponse
POST {{instance1}}/openai/v1/responses
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{apiKey1}}

{
    "model": "{{model}}",
    "input": "What is the capital of France? Answer in one word."
}


### ==========================================================================
### STEP 2 — Retrieve the response from AI Services Instance 2 using the captured ID
### ==========================================================================

@responseId = {{createResponse.response.body.id}}

# @name retrieveResponse
GET {{instance2}}/openai/v1/responses/{{responseId}}
api-key: {{apiKey2}}


### ==========================================================================
### PART B: Azure OpenAI (kind: OpenAI) Instances
### ==========================================================================

### ==========================================================================
### STEP 3 — Create a response on Azure OpenAI Instance 1
### ==========================================================================

# @name createOaiResponse
POST {{oaiInstance1}}/openai/v1/responses
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{oaiApiKey1}}

{
    "model": "{{model}}",
    "input": "What is the capital of France? Answer in one word."
}


### ==========================================================================
### STEP 4 — Retrieve the response from Azure OpenAI Instance 2 using the captured ID
### ==========================================================================

@oaiResponseId = {{createOaiResponse.response.body.id}}

# @name retrieveOaiResponse2
GET {{oaiInstance2}}/openai/v1/responses/{{oaiResponseId}}
api-key: {{oaiApiKey2}}


### ==========================================================================
### STEP 5 — Retrieve the response from Azure OpenAI Instance 3 using the captured ID
### ==========================================================================

# @name retrieveOaiResponse3
GET {{oaiInstance3}}/openai/v1/responses/{{oaiResponseId}}
api-key: {{oaiApiKey3}}
